\\\"Inter, system-ui, sans-serif\\\"\\n113|    fontSize: \\\"0.95rem\\\"\\n114|    fontWeight: 700\\n115|  small:\\n116|    fontFamily: \\\"Inter, system-ui, sans-serif\\\"\\n117|    fontSize: \\\"0.97rem\\\"\\n118|    fontWeight: 400\\n119|  detail:\\n120|    fontFamily: \\\"Inter, system-ui, sans-serif\\\"\\n121|    fontSize: \\\"0.99rem\\\"\\n122|    fontWeight: 400\\n123|  micro:\\n124|    fontFamily: \\\"Inter, system-ui, sans-serif\\\"\\n125|    fontSize: \\\"0.72rem\\\"\\n126|    fontWeight: 700\\n127|  callout-title:\\n128|    fontFamily: \\\"Inter, system-ui, sans-serif\\\"\\n129|    fontSize: \\\"1.5rem\\\"\\n130|    fontWeight: 800\\n131|rounded:\\n132|  pill: \\\"999px\\\"\\n133|  card: \\\"12px\\\"\\n134|  lg: \\\"20px\\\"\\n135|  xs: \\\"5px\\\"\\n136|  sm: \\\"6px\\\"\\n137|  r9: \\\"9px\\\"\\n138|  r10: \\\"10px\\\"\\n139|  r14: \\\"14px\\\"\\n140|  r16: \\\"16px\\\"\\n141|spacing:\\n142|  container-session: \\\"56rem\\\"\\n143|  container-portal: \\\"80rem\\\"\\n144|  gutter: \\\"1.5rem\\\"\\n145|components:\\n146|  button-pill:\\n147|    backgroundColor: \\\"transparent\\\"\\n148|    textColor: \\\"#475569\\\"\\n149|    rounded: \\\"{rounded.pill}\\\"\\n150|    padding: \\\"0.375rem 1rem\\\"\\n151|  course-card:\\n152|    backgroundColor: \\\"{colors.bg}\\\"\\n153|    textColor: \\\"#0f172a\\\"\\n154|    rounded: \\\"16px\\\"\\n155|    padding: \\\"1.5rem\\\"\\n156|  scripture:\\n157|    backgroundColor: \\\"transparent\\\"\\n158|    textColor: \\\"{colors.body}\\\"\\n159|    padding: \\\"0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.25rem\\\"\\n160|  nav-lang:\\n161|    backgroundColor: \\\"{colors.bg}\\\"\\n162|    textColor: \\\"#475569\\\"\\n163|    rounded: \\\"{rounded.pill}\\\"\\n164|    padding: \\\"0.375rem 0.875rem\\\"\\n165|---\\n166|\\n167|# Design System: Estudos Bíblicos — The Bible Project\\n168|\\n169|## Overview\\n170|\\n171|**Creative North Star: \\\"The Annotated Lecture Hall\\\"** — the reading experience of a well-set seminary reader: calm white pages, a confident near-black ink, and a single disciplined blue that marks every cross-reference, alongside a color-coded system that turns dense biblical structure (chiasms, genealogies, macro outlines) into legible diagrams. The product is a bilingual (Portuguese/English) library of course \\\"class notes\\\" from The Bible Project, so the visual job is comprehension-first: long-form reading that stays quiet, Hebrew set correctly right-to-left, and scripture quotations clearly walled off from commentary.\\n172|\\n173|Two surfaces share one identity. The **portal** (`index.html`) is a Tailwind-v3 CDN grid of course cards — the browse/discover face. The **session pages** (`<course>/modulo-N/sessao-N.html`) are Tailwind-v4 (`@tailwindcss/browser`) reading pages carrying a shared editorial stylesheet (`style.css`-equivalent inline `<style>`). Both surface a PT/EN language toggle stored in `localStorage` and gated by `html[lang]`.\\n174|\\n175|Every session page reuses the **same class vocabulary** (`h1.title`, `h2.section`, `h3.sub`, `p.body`, `.rule`, `.scripture`, `.bullets`, `.reveal`, `.page-footer`, reading-progress bar), so the courses are recolor variants of one template, not separate designs. Two documented expressions of that template exist: the **Reader template** (canonical, ~350 pages across Jonah, Joseph, Jacob, Exodus, Ezekiel, Adam-to-Noah, Messianic-Torah, Art-of-Biblical-Words, Intro-Hebrew, Heaven-and-Earth, Noah-to-Abraham, and Abraham modules 1–6) and the **Abraham cx-callout system** (the richest diagram vocabulary, used in the Abraham module). A few courses add a deliberate *course accent* (see Variants).\\n176|\\n177|**Key Characteristics:**\\n178|- Calm white reading canvas; structure via 2–4px borders and tints, not by heavy shadows.\\n179|- One blue accent (`#0284c7` sky / `#2563eb` for inline scripture refs) used sparingly: links, active language, hover borders.\\n180|- A signature **color-coded callout system** (`cx-*`) that assigns each theme a hue + tinted fill so recurring diagrams stay recognizable (Abraham module).\\n181|- Bilingual by construction: every string ships as `.lang-pt` / `.lang-en` pairs toggled together.\\n182|- Hebrew set in SBL Hebrew, forced RTL; poems and pull-quotes set in Newsreader serif for a contemplative beat.\\n183|\\n184|## Colors\\n185|\\n186|A near-monochrome ink-and-paper base, an editorial blue accent, and a fixed categorical palette for the callout/diagram system. The cx callout hues (below) are the only place multiple saturated colors appear, and they are always paired with a matching tint so they read as a system, not as decoration.\\n187|\\n188|### Primary\\n189|- **Bible-Project Sky** (`#0284c7`, Tailwind `sky-600`): the brand accent on the portal — active language pill, course-card hover border (`sky-500`), and the \\\"Start here\\\" emerald / \\\"Under construction\\\" amber badges' sibling. Used sparingly; its rarity is the point.\\n190|- **Reference Blue** (`#2563eb`, `blue-600`): the hover color of inline scripture/verse links (`.ref:hover`) and the verse-modal title text. Treat as the same accent family as Sky; the two are near-indistinguishable at a glance.\\n191|\\n192|### Neutral (Reader template — canonical)\\n193|- **Ink** (`#1a1a1a`): body text and bullet markers (`body { color:#1a1a1a }`, `ul.bullets>li:before`). Near-black, not pure black.\\n194|- **Body** (`#24262a`): paragraph (`.body`) and scripture text.\\n195|- **Heading Ink** (`#17181a`): scripture labels only.\\n196|- **Muted** (`#5b6472` / `#5b7285`): captions, footnotes, secondary labels, scripture translation tags.\\n197|- **Borders:** `#d7dde5` (`.rule`, `.table-img`), `#aeb6bf` (`.quote` rule), `#d7d7df` (nav pill), `#dfe4ea` (`.scripture` rule) — the dominant depth cues.\\n198|- **Surface** (`#f1f5f9`): nav hover fill.\\n199|- **Quote Text** (`#3a3f47`): `.quote` / `.poem` body.\\n200|- **Nav Text** (`#475569`): floating control labels.\\n201|- **Paper** (`#ffffff`): page and card backgrounds.\\n202|\\n203|### Neutral (Abraham cx-callout module)\\n204|The Abraham module's inline `<style>` uses `#17181a` ink, `#24262a` body, `#5b6472` muted, `#d7dde5`/`#e3e7ee` borders, and `#f6f8fa` inset surface — the same neutrals as the Reader template with marginally different hexes (e.g. `#17181a` vs `#1a1a1a`, `#e3e7ee` vs `#d7dde5`). Treat as the same neutral family; the drift is intra-template, not a defect.\\n205|\\n206|### Categorical — cx callout system\\n207|`cx-slate` `#6b7280`, `cx-rust` `#c0562f`, `cx-rose` `#c04a63`, `cx-blue` `#5468d4`, `cx-green` `#2e7d4e`, `cx-purple` `#8b5cf6`, `cx-tan` `#8a6d3b`, each with its `#e9ebee`/`#f7e6dd`/`#f7e0e5`/`#e4e8f9`/`#dfeee2`/`#efe2f8`/`#ece7dc` tint. Plus annotation chips `k-blue` `#3b82c4`, `k-green` `#2e6b4e`, `k-rose` `#c04a63`, `k-teal` `#0d7d8c`, `k-purple` `#7c5ad0`, `t-teal` `#0d8aa0`. Always border + matching tint.\\n208|\\n209|### Variants (course-specific accents — intentional, not defects)\\n210|- **Amber scripture accent** (Ephesians, 1 Corinthians): `blockquote` left-rule `#f59e0b` (`amber-badge`) on a `#fffbeb` (`amber-badge-bg`) tint. A deliberate course accent, distinct from the blue primary.\\n211|- **Abraham module 2–6 extended palette**: a richer per-module categorical set (teals `#0c7c99`/`#0d7685`, roses `#972a4e`/`#823221`, blues `#3b5299`/`#1d4ed8`, tans `#8a6d3b`/`#b45f06`, greens `#38761d`/`#2e8b57`, purples `#6d4cba`/`#7c3aed`). Used only inside those modules' custom diagrams; not part of the shared scale.\\n212|\\n213|### Named Rules\\n214|**The One-Blue Rule.** A single blue/sky accent carries all interactive emphasis (links, active language, hover borders). Introduce no new *interactive* hue; the cx callout and course accents are categorical/decorative, never used for links or buttons.\\n215|\\n216|**The Tint-Not-Shadow Rule.** Depth is conveyed by borders and tonal fills (`#f1f5f9`, tinted callouts), not by resting drop shadows. The only resting shadow is the 1px hairline `0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.06)` on floating nav controls; larger shadows appear only on hover/overlay.\\n217|\\n218|## Typography\\n219|\\n220|**Display Font:** Inter (with `system-ui, sans-serif` fallback) — every heading, label, UI control, and body paragraph.\\n221|**Body Font:** Inter, same stack.\\n222|**Serif Font:** Newsreader (with Georgia, serif) — reserved for poems (`.poem`) and pull-quotes (`.quote`); its italic optical size gives commentary a contemplative, \\\"readerly\\\" beat without leaving the system.\\n223|**Hebrew Font:** SBL Hebrew (with `Times New Roman`, serif) — `direction: rtl; unicode-bidi: embed` so Hebrew terms render correctly inline.\\n224|\\n225|**Character:** A precise, slightly compressed sans (Inter at 800 weight, negative letter-spacing) for a scholarly-but-modern voice; the serif body provides the only warmth. Newsreader is never a heading face here — it is a readerly accent, not a display choice.\\n226|\\n227|### Hierarchy\\n228|- **Display** (800, 2.6rem, line-height 1.08, -0.025em): session `<h1 class=\\\"title\\\">` — the lesson title only.\\n229|- **Section** (800, 1.9rem, -0.015em): `<h2 class=\\\"section\\\">` major topical breaks; 3rem top / 1.25rem bottom margin.\\n230|- **Sub** (800, 1.3rem, -0.01em): `<h3 class=\\\"sub\\\">` subsection and \\\"Reflection Question\\\" headings.\\n231|- **Body** (400, 1.05rem, line-height 1.78, color `#24262a`): default paragraph (`.body`), max readable measure inside `max-w-4xl`.\\n232|- **Label / Eyebrow** (600, 0.875rem, uppercase, 0.06em tracking, muted): scripture translation tags, footer, kickers.\\n233|- **Serif Quote** (400, 1.05rem, line-height 1.85, Newsreader): `.poem` / `.quote` blocks.\\n234|- **Hebrew Inline** (1.05em, SBL Hebrew, RTL): primary font for inline Hebrew terms.\\n235|\\n236|### Named Rules\\n237|**The Serif-Is-Readerly Rule.** Newsreader appears only for poems and pull-quotes. Never use it for headings, UI, or body paragraphs; the page stays Inter except where a quotation deserves a different register.\\n238|\\n239|**The RTL Lock Rule.** Any Hebrew string uses `.heb` with `direction: rtl`. Never strip RTL or let Hebrew terms inherit LTR flow — bilingual integrity depends on it.\\n240|\\n241|## Layout\\n242|\\n243|Two distinct spatial models from one token set:\\n244|- **Portal:** centered `max-w-7xl` (`80rem`) shell, course grid `gap-8` collapsing `md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`; cards are `rounded-2xl` with a `h-44` (`11rem`) `object-cover` cover image and a `p-6` text block.\\n245|- **Session pages:** a single reading column `max-w-4xl` (`56rem`), `px-5 md:px-10 py-12 md:py-16`, left-aligned. Content is long-form: title → `hr.rule` → subsections of heading + body + scripture blocks. Fixed top-left \\\"Back\\\" (`← Voltar`) and top-right \\\"Print / Imprimir + PT|EN\\\" controls float above the column (`print:hidden`).\\n246|\\n247|Responsive behavior is breakpoint-driven by Tailwind utilities plus two bespoke `@media` blocks (in the Abraham module): the macro-outline grid collapses `1fr` under `860px`, and the Isaiah-51 genealogy rows stack under `640px`. Vertical rhythm is generous (`1.5–2.75rem` rule spacing, `3rem` between sections) to keep long reads breathable.\\n248|\\n249|## Elevation & Depth\\n250|\\n251|Predominantly **flat**, conveyed through 2–4px borders and tonal fills rather than shadows. Surfaces at rest cast nothing except the 1px hairline on floating nav controls.\\n252|\\n253|### Shadow Vocabulary\\n254|- **Hairline (resting)** (`0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.06)`): on `.nav-btn` / floating controls — the only intentional resting shadow.\\n255|- **Hover lift — card** (`0 8px 20px -10px rgba(30,41,59,.4)`): on `.mbox` / `.cx` callouts on hover, paired with `translateY(-2px / -3px)`.\\n256|- **Hover lift — portal card** (Tailwind `shadow-xl`): on course-card hover, with `-translate-y-1` and `border-sky-500`.\\n257|- **Overlay** (`shadow-xl` + `bg-black/50` scrim): the verse modal panel (`max-w-lg rounded-lg bg-white p-6`).\\n258|\\n259|### Named Rules\\n260|**The Flat-By-Default Rule.** Reading-page surfaces are flat at rest. A drop shadow may appear only on hover/focus/overlay state (or the documented 1px nav hairline); never as a static resting style on content surfaces.\\n261|\\n262|## Shapes\\n263|\\n264|Rounded corners are explicit and modest: pills (`999px`) for language toggles and nav controls; `12px` radii for tables/images; `16–20px` for outer frames. Borders are the signature form language — hairline `1px` for tables/rules/nav, confident `3px` for Abraham-module callouts, macro boxes, and outer frames. No skewed or organic geometry; the silhouette is rectangular and calm.\\n265|\\n266|## Components\\n267|\\n268|### Buttons / Pill Controls\\n269|- **Shape:** pill (`999px`) with a `1px` slate-300 (`#cbd5e1`) border; `bg-white/90` + `backdrop-blur-xs` on floating controls (Back / Print), plain white on the language toggle (Reader) or `#fff`/`#d7d7df` on `.nav-btn`.\\n270|- **Primary (active language):** `bg-sky-600 text-white`. **Off:** `bg-white text-slate-600 hover:bg-slate-100` (portal) or `bg-white text-slate-600 hover:bg-slate-50` (session).\\n271|- **Hover/Focus:** color shift + subtle bg change; `transition-colors`.\\n272|\\n273|### Course Card (portal)\\n274|- **Shape:** `rounded-2xl` (16px), `border-2` slate-200, white bg, `overflow-hidden`.\\n275|- **Cover:** `h-44 w-full object-cover`.\\n276|- **Body:** title `text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900` → `group-hover:text-sky-600`; reference label `text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500`; description `text-sm text-slate-600`.\\n277|- **Hover:** border-sky-500, `shadow-xl`, `-translate-y-1`.\\n278|- **Status badge:** pill, top-right — emerald-100 bg / emerald-700 text (\\\"Start here\\\") or amber-100 bg / amber-700 text (\\\"Under construction\\\").\\n279|\\n280|### Scripture Block\\n281|- **Style:** `border-left: 4px solid #dfe4ea`, padding `0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.25rem`, `transition: border-color .2s`.\\n282|- **Label:** `font-weight 800` ink (`#17181a`); **type tag:** muted 700 (`NVI` / `NASB`).\\n283|- **Text:** `1.05rem`, line-height `1.8`, color `#24262a`. Optional inset box (`#f6f8fa` in Abraham module).\\n284|- **Hover:** border-left shifts to `#9aa7b8`.\\n285|\\n286|### Quote / Poem\\n287|- **Style:** `border-left: 4px solid #aeb6bf`, padding `.4rem 0 .4rem 1.25rem`; text `#3a3f47`, italic, Newsreader when `.poem`.\\n288|- **Variant:** Ephesians/1 Corinthians use `#f59e0b` amber rule on `blockquote` over `#fffbeb` tint.\\n289|\\n290|### Signature Component — Color-Coded Callout (`cx-*`, Abraham module)\\n291|The defining pattern: a `3px` colored border + matching tinted fill, a white-on-color tag pill, and a hover lift. Reused so recurring structures (chiasms, themes) stay visually consistent.\\n292|- **cx-slate** `#6b7280` / `#e9ebee` · **cx-rust** `#c0562f` / `#f7e6dd` · **cx-rose** `#c04a63` / `#f7e0e5` · **cx-blue** `#5468d4` / `#e4e8f9` · **cx-green** `#2e7d4e` / `#dfeee2` · **cx-purple** `#8b5cf6` / `#efe2f8` · **cx-tan** `#8a6d3b` / `#ece7dc`.\\n293|- Hover: `box-shadow 0 12px 26px -16px rgba(23,24,26,.45)` + `translateY(-2px)`.\\n294|\\n295|### Verse Modal\\n296|Injected by the shared `js/verse-modal.js`. Fixed `inset-0 z-50` `bg-black/50` scrim; panel `w-full max-w-lg rounded-lg bg-white p-6 shadow-xl`; title `text-xl font-bold text-slate-900`; body `max-h-[60vh] overflow-y-auto text-slate-700`. Fetches from `bible-api.com` on `.ref` / `.verse-link` click.\\n297|\\n298|### Reading Progress Bar\\n299|Fixed top, `height: 3px`, full width, `bg #1a1a1a` (Reader) / `#17181a` (Abraham), `transform: scaleX(0→1)` driven by scroll. `aria-hidden`; hidden in print.\\n300|\\n301|### Tables (`.doc-table` / `.table-img`)\\n302|`border-collapse: separate`, `3px` border `#d9dee6`, `rounded-14`, `overflow: hidden`; or a 1px `#d7dde5` border with `rounded-12` for image tables. Header `th` `bg #e2e6eb`, `font-weight 800`, ink; rows hover `#f8fafc` / `#f1f5f9`.\\n303|\\n304|### Navigation\\n305|Floating controls + the PT/EN split toggle (documented under Buttons). Mobile: controls stay fixed top-left/right; grid collapses to one column.\\n306|\\n307|## Do's and Don'ts\\n308|\\n309|### Do:\\n310|- **Do** keep Inter for all UI, headings, and body; reserve Newsreader for `.poem` / `.quote` only.\\n311|- **Do** set Hebrew in `.heb` with RTL — never let Hebrew terms flow LTR.\\n312|- **Do** convey depth with borders and `#f1f5f9`/`#f6f8fa` tints; the only resting shadow is the 1px nav hairline.\\n313|- **Do** reuse the `cx-*` hue set consistently for callouts; pair each border with its tinted fill.\\n314|- **Do** keep session reading width at `max-w-4xl` and preserve the PT/EN toggle + reading-progress bar.\\n315|\\n316|### Don't:\\n317|- **Don't** introduce a new *interactive* accent color — links, active language, and hover borders stay in the blue/sky family.\\n318|- **Don't** apply resting drop shadows to reading-page content surfaces (cards, callouts, tables).\\n319|- **Don't** drop or restyle the bilingual `.lang-pt` / `.lang-en` toggle; it is the product's core control.\\n320|- **Don't** use Newsreader or SBL Hebrew as a display/UI face.\\n321|- **Don't** break `print` rules (`@media print` hides progress bar/controls) — print fidelity is a requirement.\\n322|# DESIGN.md — Estrutura das Sessões de Curso\\n323|\\n324|Este repositório contém cursos bíblicos (BibleProject Classroom). Cada curso tem\\n325|um PDF de `teacher-notes` e sessões HTML bilíngues (PT/EN) no padrão **abraao**\\n326|(curso de referência considerado \\\"terminado igual ao PDF\\\").\\n327|\\n328|## Estrutura de pastas\\n329|\\n330|```\\n331|<curso>/\\n332|  <curso>-teacher-notes.pdf     # fonte canônica do conteúdo\\n333|  index.html                    # índice dos módulos (header + toggle PT/EN)\\n334|  modulo-N/\\n335|    sessao-N.html               # NÃO em subpasta (write_file direto)\\n336|    img/sessao-N/pK-vector.png # imagens vetoriais por página do PDF (quando houver)\\n337|  js/verse-modal.js             # modal de versículo (compartilhado)\\n338|```\\n339|\\n340|Mapeamento PDF→sessão é feito pelo marcador `Session N:` no teacher-notes.\\n341|\\n342|## Padrão abraao (golden)\\n343|\\n344|Template reutilizado em `abraao/modulo-1/sessao-1.html`:\\n345|\\n346|- **HEAD/CSS**: fontes Inter + Newsreader, `.heb` (hebraico), `.ref`, `.scripture`,\\n347|  `.cx` (quiasmo), `.doc-table`, `.v-outer`, `.title`, `.section`, `.sub`,\\n348|  `.body`, `.reveal`, barra `#reading-progress`.\\n349|- **NAV**: botão `Voltar` → `index.html`, `Imprimir` (`window.print()`),\\n350|  toggle `PT`/`EN` (`setLang`, `localStorage` `sN-lang`).\\n351|- **CORPO**: `<div class=\\\"max-w-4xl mx-auto ...\\\">` → `<h1 class=\\\"title reveal\\\">`\\n352|  → `<hr>` → blocos `h2.section`/`h3.sub`/`p.body`/`.scripture`/`.heb`/`.ref`/`.cx`,\\n353|  cada um com `<span class=\\\"lang-pt\\\">` + `<span class=\\\"lang-en\\\">`.\\n354|- **TAIL**: script `setLang()`, `#reading-progress` (scroll), `IntersectionObserver`\\n355|  reveal, `verse-modal.js`. **Zero `<img>`** nas sessões abraao (texto curado).\\n356|\\n357|## Checklist de sessão completa (`SESSAO_CHECKLIST.md`)\\n358|\\n359|Uma sessão está completa quando satisfaz:\\n360|\\n361|1. **Header/estrutura** — `<title>` correto, `Voltar`, `Imprimir`, toggle PT/EN,\\n362|   `#reading-progress`, `verse-modal.js`, `page-footer`.\\n363|2. **Texto bilíngue** — `lang-en` + `lang-pt` por bloco; EN reproduz o PDF, PT traduzido.\\n364|3. **Todo o texto do PDF** — cada frase do teacher-notes da sessão aparece no HTML\\n365|   (PT ou EN); sem lixo de cabeçalho (`Class Notes:`, `N of M`, `Session N:`).\\n366|4. **Todas as imagens do PDF da sessão** — `<img>` contagem == imagens nas páginas\\n367|   do PDF (`img/sessao-N/pK-vector.png`).\\n368|5. **Citações** — formato `Autor (AAAA). Título. Editora.` (Wright, Pennington, etc).\\n369|\\n370|## Verificação\\n371|\\n372|`check_session_coverage.py` auto-mapeia PDF→sessão e 